# What this repository's release needs that another's does not. See propensive/.github, which
# holds the workflow and the script; a release is cut by `git tag -s X.Y.Z && git push --tags`.
#
# Soundness declares no `val soundnessVersion`: `publishVersion` is driven entirely by
# SOUNDNESS_RELEASE_VERSION, which release.sh exports from the tag, so there is no pin to agree
# with and no version to bump before tagging.

name       soundness
title      Soundness

# The JVM surface first, then Scala.js, before `release.stage` runs. `release.stage` alone starts
# the JVM, Scala.js and Native compilers of the root module simultaneously on a cold daemon, and
# those three race on dotty's JVM-global jar-lookup cache: one can see a partial view of the
# standard library and fail capture checking on a module that compiles cleanly a moment later.
# Compiling the aggregates first leaves the caches warm before anything runs concurrently.
build      soundness.all.compile soundness.js.compile

# Every released module must resolve to the tag before anything leaves the machine. Both compiler
# plugins (which shipped a stale 0.63.0 inside the 0.64.0 release), plus a component and its
# crosses; the environment makes all modules resolve identically, so a few suffice.
probes     beneficence.plugin larceny.plugin rudiments.core rudiments.core.js rudiments.core.native

# The migration notes must be finalised: the release PR renames pending.md to <version>.md, and
# the first change after the release starts a new pending.md. A surviving pending.md means that
# PR has not merged, so the tag names a commit whose notes are still unreleased.
migration  doc/migration

# The trust boundary is the signed attestation note on refs/notes/ci-attestation, not the runner.
verify     ./mill groupCheck.validate
verify     ./etc/ci/verify-attest.sh
